KG42.register("clusters-4c21abdd5f71f618c840e724",{"id":"49-residential_shared_storage_market::v142-d-CL004","paper":"49-residential_shared_storage_market","label":"Measurement of the seller's P2P transaction fee and the price-floor interface","record":{"cluster_id":"v142-d-CL004","label":"Measurement of the seller's P2P transaction fee and the price-floor interface","market_meaning":"Measure the transaction-fee term in the seller's profit using the seller's bilateral transaction volume, time-period length, and P2P transaction-cost rate; the rate includes the network-use fee and aggregator service fee. The same cost parameter also enters the existing seller price floor. The complete scope of this Rule-Cluster is limited to the fee term and its pricing interface.","mechanism_ids":["v141-a-M01"],"market_types":["LEM"],"process_stages":["settlement","pricing"],"scope_disposition":"compatible","scope_explanation":"The fee term and the price floor reference the seller's P2P transaction quantity and transaction-cost parameter in the same model, and their local uses remain independent. General parameters are not replaced by test-case numerical values; complete receipt and payment, fee allocation, and settlement arrangements remain outside the known scope of this Rule-Cluster.","assembly_status":"assembled","boundary_rationale":"This Rule-Cluster has explicit transaction-volume and rate inputs, seller fee calculation, and profit-deduction meaning, and can serve as an independent accounting rule. The pricing side only provides quantity and cost interfaces; it neither re-assumes equilibrium solving nor expands the fee term into a complete settlement system.","chain_bindings":[{"chain_id":"v141-c-R010","ownership":"primary","role":"core","rationale":"Provide the composition of the transaction fee and the volume-based charging term in the seller's profit, constituting the independent result of this Rule-Cluster."},{"chain_id":"v141-c-R008","ownership":"shared","role":"interface","rationale":"Provide the transaction-volume output and the interface through which the same transaction cost enters the price floor, without adding fees or recalculating price rules."}],"connections":[{"connection_id":"v142-d-CL004-L001","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R008","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R010","kind":"quantity_interface","from_refs":["v141-c-R008::x::v141-c-R008-x-p","v141-c-R008::theta::v141-c-R008-theta-Delta-t"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R010::x::v141-c-R010-X001","v141-c-R010::theta::v141-c-R010-T002","v141-c-R010::phi::v141-c-R010-C002"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E11","v141-b-g01-E13","v141-b-g01-E21","v141-b-g02-e034"],"rationale":"The bilateral transaction volume output by equilibrium and the same time-period length constitute the measurement inputs for the seller fee term; this is only an existing quantity interface and does not add settlement timing."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-CL004-L002","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R010","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R008","kind":"functional_coupling","from_refs":["v141-c-R010::theta::v141-c-R010-T001","v141-c-R010::phi::v141-c-R010-C002"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R008::theta::v141-c-R008-theta-lambda-cost","v141-c-R008::phi::v141-c-R008-C002"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E11","v141-b-g01-E13","v141-b-g03-e04"],"rationale":"In the source text, the same transaction cost is both deducted in the seller's profit and included in the detailed price floor; the two uses are complementary and do not create a second charging obligation."}],"object_mappings":[{"mapping_id":"v142-d-CL004-M001","kind":"same_quantity","member_refs":["v141-c-R008::x::v141-c-R008-x-p","v141-c-R010::x::v141-c-R010-X001"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E11","v141-b-g01-E13","v141-b-g01-E21","v141-b-g02-e034"],"rationale":"The bilateral transaction volume for the same seller, buyer, and time period is respectively the equilibrium allocation quantity and the fee-measurement base, retaining two local roles."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-CL004-M002","kind":"same_quantity","member_refs":["v141-c-R008::theta::v141-c-R008-theta-lambda-cost","v141-c-R010::theta::v141-c-R010-T001"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E13","v141-b-g01-E21","v141-b-g03-e04"],"rationale":"The same definition and model scope support the identity association of the transaction-cost parameter, but its roles as a component of the price floor and as a basis for fee accounting are retained separately."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-CL004-M003","kind":"same_quantity","member_refs":["v141-c-R008::theta::v141-c-R008-theta-Delta-t","v141-c-R010::theta::v141-c-R010-T002"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E10","v141-b-g01-E21","v141-b-g02-e034"],"rationale":"Both are the time-period length of this multi-period model, used respectively for price decomposition and fee-term measurement, without rewriting the original parameter object."}],"gaps":[{"gap_id":"v142-d-CL004-G001","category":"unverified_source","description":"The fee term and cost composition rely on unaudited B transcriptions; assembled only means that these references form a coherent candidate within the defined accounting scope and does not mean scientific approval.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R010","v141-c-R008"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R010::phi::v141-c-R010-C001","v141-c-R010::phi::v141-c-R010-C002"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E11","v141-b-g01-E13","v141-b-g01-E14","v141-b-g02-e034","v141-b-g03-e04"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Manually check the fee sign, summation range, time-period length, and cost composition in the seller objective, and maintain the current unaudited evidence status."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-CL004-G002","category":"upstream_missing","description":"The frozen Rule-Chain provides the transaction-fee term in the seller's profit, but does not include the split between network fees and service fees, the actual allocation of receipts, or settlement timing. The existing references cannot cover a complete payment system.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R010"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R010::phi::v141-c-R010-C001","v141-c-R010::phi::v141-c-R010-C002"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E11","v141-b-g01-E13","v141-b-g01-E14"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"If expansion into a complete settlement rule is needed, upstream should find and record the actual receipt-payment and fee-allocation clauses; content not provided in the source text remains blank, and the current fee-term scope is maintained."}]},"rule_refs":["49-residential_shared_storage_market::v141-c-R010","49-residential_shared_storage_market::v141-c-R008"],"unresolved_rule_refs":[],"node_ids":["COMP-4c1817f6cddf8a9c","COMP-58a3c8caf66a5d40","COMP-8a45c72bc028dfa5"]});
